61:The script reads workspace manifests directly (pnpm-workspace.yaml, package.json workspaces, lerna, nx, turbo, go.work, Cargo.toml) and expands trailing-`*` (single-level) and `**` (recursive) globs — only directories containing `package.json` are kept as workspace candidates — then `.gitmodules` for submodules, then probes first-level subdirectories not already covered for nested `.git`. It excludes `node_modules`, `dist`, `vendor`, and hidden directories. go.work and Cargo members are trusted as explicit paths and bypass the `package.json` filter. See `scripts/scan-packages.mjs` for the full rule set and `scripts/scan-packages.test.ts` for fixture-backed examples.
== 4. spec 条目 ==
10:- coverage-config: `coverage` is a project-level config field with `threshold` (integer 0–100, default 90, strict `>`) and a `languages` map of `{ format, command? }`; format accepts exactly `go-coverprofile`, `lcov`, `jacoco-xml`, and `cobertura-xml`. Unknown subfields, invalid formats, and `<…>` placeholders outside the closed `<worktree>` / `<profile>` / `<base-ref>` whitelist fail loud. Built-in languages (go/typescript/javascript/python/rust/c/cpp/java/kotlin) fall back to `LANGUAGE_DEFAULTS` when unconfigured, with extension detection from the single `EXTENSION_LANGUAGE` map; a non-built-in language without a configured entry stays on the unsupported consistency fallback, where the configured threshold still applies to self-reported numbers. `workloom-packages-scan` proposes defaults for detected languages through the `workloom-config-edit` skill
